    "new_defect_established": false,
    "result": "The frozen Phase D regression versus naive is reproducible and is not explained by environment drift. Ridge is strongly tail-sensitive but remains worse than naive after removing its dominant January loss cluster. HistGB underperformance is smaller but more systematic across folds, periods, and regimes. The earlier smoke-to-Phase-D performance flip is real as an observed checkpoint change but is not causally attributable from these checkpoints because methodology and data changed simultaneously."
  },
